---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectFeed from "../components/react/ProjectFeed";
---
<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero"><svg class="scribble" style="left:-30px;bottom:40px;width:210px" viewBox="0 0 220 120" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 72c34-68 113-65 162-24 42 36-34 83-84 53-43-26-6-82 60-79 30 2 57 17 72 36" fill="none" stroke="#244766" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><div class="shell hero-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Independent software studio · Tampa Bay</span><h1 class="display">We make digital tools <span>feel human.</span></h1><p class="hero-copy">Apps, websites, and e-commerce built for creative businesses and creative people—with clear thinking, sturdy code, and the kind of care you can feel.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/contact">Bring us a project <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/work">See the work</a></div></div><aside class="work-ticket" aria-label="Sudo Create work order"><div class="ticket-label"><span>Work order № 1984</span><span>Open</span></div><p class="ticket-title">Built to be used.</p><p class="muted">Good software should feel like a familiar tool: easy to pick up, dependable when the work gets real, and unmistakably yours.</p><div class="rule" style="margin-top:1.1rem;padding-top:.8rem"><div class="ticket-label" style="border:0;padding:0"><span>Apps · Web · Commerce</span><span>EST. 2026</span></div></div><div class="punches" aria-hidden="true">{Array.from({length:9}).map(()=><i></i>)}</div></aside></div></section>
  <div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true"><span>Strategy ✦ Design ✦ Development ✦ Apps ✦ Websites ✦ E-commerce ✦ Built with care ✦ Strategy ✦ Design ✦ Development ✦ Apps ✦ Websites ✦ E-commerce ✦</span></div>
  <section class="section band"><div class="shell"><div class="split-heading"><span class="eyebrow">The shop floor</span><div><h2 class="display">What we build.</h2><p>Practical digital work for people with taste, ideas, and a business to run. No mysterious process. No off-the-shelf personality.</p></div></div><div class="service-ledger"><a class="service-row" href="/services#apps"><span class="service-number">01 / APP</span><h3>Custom apps</h3><p>Purpose-built products, internal tools, and prototypes shaped around the way your people actually work.</p></a><a class="service-row" href="/services#websites"><span class="service-number">02 / WEB</span><h3>Websites</h3><p>Distinctive, fast sites that make your business easier to understand—and easier to choose.</p></a><a class="service-row" href="/services#commerce"><span class="service-number">03 / SHOP</span><h3>E-commerce</h3><p>Thoughtful storefronts and buying flows that serve the brand without getting in the customer’s way.</p></a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="split-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Selected work</span><div><h2 class="display">Made for real life.</h2><p>Digital products and places with a clear job to do. The CMS can add and reorder projects here without changing the frontend.</p></div></div><ProjectFeed client:load limit={3}/></div></section>
  <section class="section band"><div class="shell"><div class="split-heading"><span class="eyebrow">How it goes</span><div><h2 class="display">A handshake, then a plan.</h2><p>You’ll always know what we’re making, why it matters, and what happens next.</p></div></div><div class="process-grid"><article class="process-card"><h3>Pull up a chair.</h3><p>We start with the business, the people, and the stubborn problem—not a list of trendy features.</p></article><article class="process-card"><h3>Make it tangible.</h3><p>We map the work, prototype the important parts, and show decisions early enough to improve them.</p></article><article class="process-card"><h3>Build it sturdy.</h3><p>We ship clean, maintainable work and leave you with a system you understand and can keep using.</p></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell founder-grid"><div class="portrait-frame"><img src="/headshot.jpg" alt="Shawn Papineau, founder of Sudo Create"/></div><div class="founder-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Your neighbor in software</span><h2 class="display">Small studio.<br/>Full attention.</h2><p>Sudo Create is Shawn Papineau’s independent software studio. It brings the curiosity of a creative practice and the accountability of a good trade: listen closely, explain the work, and build something worth putting your name on.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/about">Meet Sudo Create →</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><div class="shell contact-card"><div class="split-heading" style="margin:0"><span class="eyebrow">Have a project?</span><div><h2 class="display">Let’s make something useful.</h2><p>Tell us what you’re trying to build, fix, or finally get out of your head.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/contact">Start the conversation →</a></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
